findings.body:
The `isCurrentUser` flag changed from "the filter is exactly `[self]`" to "the filter includes self". The FORBIDDEN guard only throws when `!areUserIdsWithinUserOrgOrTeam && !isCurrentUser`, so a filter of `[self, victimId]` passes whenever `isCurrentUser` is true. The booking queries then filter on the caller's full list, which includes `victimId`. A non-admin can therefore list another user's bookings by adding their own ID to the filter.

::code{file="packages/trpc/server/routers/viewer/bookings/get.handler.ts" lines="144-160"}

::callout{type="security"}
The check on line 149 is the only gate on `filters.userIds`. Booking queries at line 170 (`Booking.userId in filters.userIds`) and the attendee-email query that follows use the unchecked list. Each query needs the guarded set, not the raw input.

::suggestion{file="packages/trpc/server/routers/viewer/bookings/get.handler.ts" lines="144-156"}
